It should keep an inline comment after text
<p>text {# hello world #}</p>

It should keep an inline comment between text
<p>text {# hello world #} more text{# glued #}, the end</p>

It should not parse the contents of a comment
<p>text {# {% if x %} {{ y #}</p>

It should not parse HTML or quotes in a comment
<ul><li>it {# isn't </li> <script> #} here</li><li>there {# <div class="a> #}</li></ul>

It should not parse closing and branching tags in a comment
{% if a %}text {# {% else %} {% endif %} #}{% else %}other {# {% endif %} #}{% endif %}

It should not parse raw tags in a comment
<p>text {# {% verbatim %} #} {{ x|upper }}</p>

It should keep the layout of a multi-line comment after text
<p>A paragraph.
{#
first line
  second line

last line
#}
</p>

It should keep the layout of a multi-line comment between text
<p>before {#
first line
last line
#} after</p>

It should fill the text around an inline comment
<p>A very long paragraph that goes past the print width with a {# spaced comment #} word after it</p>

It should strip whitespace when breaking around a comment without whitespace around it
<p>A very long paragraph that goes past the print width with a{# glued comment here #}word after it</p>

It should keep the whitespace control of a comment after text
<p>a {#~ b ~#} c</p>

It should collapse an empty comment after text
<p>text {##}</p>

It should respect a prettier-ignore comment after text
<div>text
{# prettier-ignore #}
<b>{{a|b}}</b></div>

It should not treat a comment opener in an expression as a comment
<p>text {{ foo("#{x}") }}</p>
<p>text {{ "{#{x}}" }}</p>
<p>text {{ foo({'a': '{#'}) }} {# comment #}</p>
{% set x = '{# not a comment #}' %}

It should not treat a comment opener in a raw element as a comment
<script>
const a = "{#"; const b = {#x: 1};
</script>

It should not treat a comment opener in a raw tag as a comment
{% verbatim %}text {# it's{% endverbatim %} text {# {% verbatim %} #}

It should parse comments in quoted attribute values
<a class="a {# {{ b }} #} c" id='d {# it's #}' title="{# f #} g">x</a>

It should parse comments in unquoted attribute values
<a class=a{# it's #}b>x</a>

It should parse comments in attribute names
<a data-{# it's #}a="1" data-b{# c #}>x</a>

It should parse comments between attributes
<a data-a {# it's #} data-b {# <b> #}data-c="1">x</a>
